  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Adaptaci&#xf3;n al Cambio Clim&#xe1;tico</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging Economic Investment through Alliances Project (Infrastructure)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Guatemala):  In 2024, the Leveraging Economic Investment through Alliances (LEIA) activity will advance Guatemala&apos;s capacity to address vulnerabilities posed by climate change by promoting climate-resilient infrastructure projects as part of the Resilient Critical Infrastructure directive. By connecting existing and new capital investors to these initiatives, LEIA will identify systemic barriers to infrastructure development and advocate for targeted reforms to improve processes and policies. Technical assistance will support risk assessments, hazard mapping, and resilience planning to ensure infrastructure investments incorporate climate-smart principles..The activity will also focus on building the capacity of national and local government entities, such as the Ministry of Communications, Infrastructure, and Housing (MICIVI) and the National Agency of Partnerships for the Development of Infrastructure (ANADIE), enabling them to conduct disaster risk assessments and integrate climate resilience into planning. Community-led assessments will further promote local ownership of solutions while addressing vulnerabilities in critical infrastructure. With FY 2024 funding, LEIA will support investments across sectors like transportation, water, and sanitation, reinforcing the foundational role of infrastructure in driving sustainable, broad-based economic growth. The activity directly supports CDCS 2020-2025, the Root Causes Strategy Pillar 1, JSP Objective 2.2, IR 1.3 of USAID&apos;s Climate Strategy, and Pillar III of the Digital Ecosystem Framework, aligning with Guatemala&apos;s Digital Ecosystem Country Framework and GEEA Priority 3?....</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Adaptaci&#xf3;n al Cambio Clim&#xe1;tico</narrative>
  </description>
